 controlled trial</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>2006</year><volume>244</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16794386</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dittrick</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Ridl</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuhn</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>McCarty</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Routine ilioinguinal nerve excision in inguinal hernia repairs</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>2004</year><volume>188</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>736</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15619492</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ravichandran</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalambe</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><name><surname>Pain</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pilot randomized controlled study of preservation or division of ilioinguinal nerve in open mesh repair of inguinal hernia</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>87</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>1166</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10971422</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amid</surname><given-names>PK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A 1-stage surgical treatment for post herniorrhaphy neuropathic pain: triple neurectomy and proximal end implantation without mobilization of the cord</article-title><source>Arch Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>137</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>100</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11772226</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Starling</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Nyhus</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Condon</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genitofemoral Neuralgia</article-title><source>Hernia</source><year>1995</year><edition>4th ed</edition><publisher-loc>Philadelphia</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lippincott</publisher-name><fpage>278</fpage><lpage>82</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heise</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Starling</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mesh inguinodynia: a new clinical syndrome after inguinal herniorrhaphy?</article-title><source>J Am Coll Surg</source><year>1998</year><volume>187</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>514</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9809568</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="web"><comment>Surgical-tutor.org.uk. Free on-line resource. Groin hernias. Available from: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.surgical-tutor.org.uk/default-home.htm"/>. Last accessed May 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="b24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Angelos</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Darosa</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bentram</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherman</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Residents seeking informed consent: Are they adequately knowledgeable?</article-title><source>Curr Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>59</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16093119</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>